<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key><string>com.gascity.claude-pool-account</string>

  <!-- ga-8hcnvb.1 / ga-8hcnvb.2 — the headless pool's Claude account as DATA, moved at 100% by a script that spends
       no credit. One run a minute: LOOK at the pool's own tmux panes (no API call); only if a pool session shows claude's
       limit screen - the modal on a session's first hit ("What do you want to do?" / "Stop and wait for limit to reset"),
       the inline "You've hit your ... limit" envelope on every later one - is the active account asked ONCE (a rejected
       429 is free) and, if it is rejected, the pool's Keychain item is moved to the next account of the order. There is NO utilization threshold: the pool moves when the limit was hit, not before (Athos 04/10).
       The one other thing asked, on every run that did not ask that, is free and says nothing about balance: whether the
       active account's KEY is still accepted (count_tokens, never billed, never serves a generation). A revoked or expired
       key never shows on a pane (a session prints a 401 "API Error" line, not a limit screen), so this check needs no pane:
       a refused key fails over in the same run, even with tmux down.
       At the stored reset time of a previously exhausted account the pool moves back, with no probe of it. Sessions that
       were on the modal of the replaced credential are sent ONE Escape (the modal only, pool panes only, 45 s after the item changed;
       see "The Escape exception" in docs/claude-pool-account.md). Live pool sessions follow the item within ~40 s.

       A run that cannot tell (network, 5xx) or cannot look (tmux down) concludes nothing about the limit and moves nothing for
       it (a key the free check finds REFUSED still fails over: it does not need the panes). Mayor and crews are not
       touched and never pressed: they run the plain `claude` / `claude-rc` providers, which never see the pool item.
       The daemon talks to the city's tmux server (`tmux -L gascity`): `tmux` is in /opt/homebrew/bin, on the PATH below.

       KILL SWITCHES (no reload needed): touch /Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/no-pool-account — the daemon
       stops acting and new pool launches stop pointing at the item; touch .../.gc/no-pool-unstick — it still decides
       and switches but never presses a key. See docs/claude-pool-account.md.

       ACTIVATION is deliberately a separate, human step (merged != live): copy this file to ~/Library/LaunchAgents
       and `launchctl load` it AFTER the script exists on main. The first run (<= 60 s later) creates the item.
       Python is /usr/bin/python3 like the other city daemons (3.9: the script is tested on that interpreter). -->

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>/usr/bin/python3</string>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/packs/town-deltas/assets/scripts/claude-pool-account.py</string>
    <string>run-once</string>
  </array>

  <key>WorkingDirectory</key>
  <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>

  <!-- 60 s > one run (a tmux scan, and at most a probe or two of ~1 s; the script holds a flock, so a slow run is never doubled). -->
  <key>StartInterval</key><integer>60</integer>
  <key>RunAtLoad</key><false/>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/claude-pool-account-launchd.out</string>
  <key>StandardErrorPath</key><string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq/.gc/logs/claude-pool-account-launchd.err</string>

  <key>EnvironmentVariables</key>
  <dict>
    <!-- ~/.local/bin: `secret` (the vault). /usr/bin: `security`. -->
    <key>PATH</key>
    <string>/opt/homebrew/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/sbin:/Users/athos/.local/bin</string>
    <key>HOME</key>
    <string>/Users/athos</string>
    <!-- claude asks the Keychain for account $USER; launchd does not always set it. -->
    <key>USER</key>
    <string>athos</string>
    <key>GC_CITY_PATH</key>
    <string>/Users/athos/gt/.gascity-gastown-hq</string>
  </dict>
</dict>
</plist>
